cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HEAPY in your research, please cite this software in your
  reference list and state the version used in your methods section.
type: software
version: "0.2.3"
date-released: "2026-10-10"
title: "HEAPY: A Python toolkit for data reduction, timing analysis, and spectral extraction of X-ray and gamma-ray transients"
authors:
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Jun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5485-5042"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jyangch/heapy"
url: "https://github.com/jyangch/heapy"
abstract: >-
  HEAPY is a Python toolkit for data reduction, timing analysis, and
  spectral extraction of X-ray and gamma-ray transients. It provides mission archive data retrieval,
  event reduction, light-curve extraction, background fitting, signal
  detection, OGIP spectral products, duration and spectral-lag measurements,
  and localization tools for high-energy astrophysics research.
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - high-energy astrophysics
  - gamma-ray bursts
  - X-ray transients
  - timing analysis
  - spectral analysis
